              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner (Edward G. McDonough), petitioner Edward G. McDonough filed a Section\u202f1983 lawsuit alleging that the respondent, Youel Smith, pursued criminal proceedings based on fabricated evidence."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-295c6e85cd63-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The malicious prosecution claim in the lawsuit was dismissed by the Second Circuit and the dismissal remains unchallenged."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-295c6e85cd63-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States, as amicus curiae, argues that the analogous common\u2011law tort is Heck malicious prosecution, and that favorable termination is an element of the Section\u202f1983 claim."
      }
    ],
